<h1>FamilyHub Privacy Policy</h1>
<p>Effective date: 23 November 2026</p>

<h2>1. About FamilyHub</h2>
<p>FamilyHub is a privately operated household management
system hosted on a household-controlled Raspberry Pi.
It is made available to household members and people
authorised by the household administrator.</p>

<h2>2. Information accessed</h2>
<p>When a user connects a Google Account, FamilyHub uses
Google OAuth authorisation and the permissions approved
by that user. Depending on those permissions, information
may include the Google account email address, calendar
names, calendar identifiers and event information such as
titles, dates, times, descriptions, locations and attendees.</p>

<h2>3. How Google information is used</h2>
<p>Google user data is used only to connect the account,
retrieve and synchronise authorised calendars, display
calendar information within the private FamilyHub system
and maintain the authorised connection.</p>
<p>FamilyHub does not sell Google user data or use it for
advertising, targeted advertising or profiling.</p>

<h2>4. Storage and security</h2>
<p>FamilyHub is self-hosted on the household's Raspberry Pi.
Application records and calendar information are stored
on that system. Google authorisation tokens are encrypted
before being stored by the application.</p>
<p>The household administrator is responsible for maintaining
the system, controlling access and protecting local backups.</p>

<h2>5. Sharing</h2>
<p>FamilyHub does not sell Google user data or share it with
advertising networks or data brokers. Calendar information
may be visible to people authorised to use the household's
FamilyHub installation.</p>
<p>Information may be disclosed where required by law.</p>

<h2>6. Retention and deletion</h2>
<p>Connected-account information is retained while the
connection is in use. Users can revoke FamilyHub's Google
access through their
<a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">
Google Account permissions</a>.</p>
<p>The household administrator can remove the connection
and associated information from FamilyHub. Local backups
may retain information until those backups are deleted.</p>

<h2>7. User choices</h2>
<p>Connecting a Google Account is optional. Users can revoke
access at any time and can ask the household administrator
to remove their connection and associated locally stored
information.</p>

<h2>8. Third-party services</h2>
<p>Google services are operated independently and are subject
to Google's own terms and privacy policies.</p>

<h2>9. Changes</h2>
<p>This policy may be updated if FamilyHub's features or
data practices change. The current version will be published
at this address.</p>

<h2>10. Contact</h2>
<p>For questions about information held in FamilyHub, contact
the household administrator using the contact details
provided when access to FamilyHub was granted.</p>
